Add a customconfig.sh file under the bash/dev-config directory.

Copy the following code snippet into it, and set the required variables:
if [ "$MSYSTEM" = "MINGW64" ]; then
    prod_kube_config_file_path="/q/kube-config"
    WINDOWS_WORKSPACE_DIR="/q/workspace"
    EXPLORER_COMPATIBLE_WORKSPACE_DIR="Q:\\workspace"
else
    prod_kube_config_file_path="/mnt/q/kube-config"
    WSL_WORKSPACE_DIR="${HOME}/workspace"
fi

DEVOPS_NEW_BRANCH_USERNAME_PREFIX=""

If you want to use a Git shortcut (e.g., g), set the prefix like this:
DEVOPS_NEW_BRANCH_USERNAME_PREFIX="<alias>"

Note: If customconfig.sh is missing, bash/config.sh will set the default values.

Recommendations:
- store kubeconfig for production is stored in a separate file
- use the default kubeconfig file for local development
